    <statement><p>Simplify the expression  <m>\displaystyle{\ \frac{2x-1}{x-2}+ \frac{1-x}{x-2}\ }</m>.</p>
<p>The answer has the form of <m>\displaystyle{\frac{f(x)}{g(x)}}</m> where</p>
<p><m>f(x)</m> = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/> and</p>
<p><m>g(x)</m> = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>x</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>x-2</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p><m>\displaystyle{\begin{aligned}\frac{2x-1}{x-2}+ \frac{1-x}{x-2} 
    \amp = \frac{(2x-1)+(1-x)}{x-2}\\
    \amp =\frac{{x}}{{x-2}} \end{aligned}}</m></p>
</solution>
